// Compact bipartite network simplex for the assignment problem.
// Representation: a spanning tree on 2n nodes (n rows + n columns) with 2n-1 edges.
// Rooted at row 0. Each non-root node stores parent, thread (preorder next),
// reverse thread, subtree size, potential, flow on the parent edge, and whether
// the parent edge is oriented row->col (always true for bipartite if parent is the other part...
// not necessarily: parent may be same? no, bipartite tree edges always cross).
//
// Initialization: greedy matching extended to a tree by connecting unmatched columns
// to row 0 with zero flow, and unmatched rows to an arbitrary matched column.
//
// Pivot: Dantzig pricing with candidate list.
#include <cstdint>
#include <vector>
#include <cmath>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cstdio>
#include <cstring>

